==In animation==
==={{aniseries|PTS}}===
===={{aniseries|GS}}====
In the American promotional video ''[[Pokémon Insider: The Video]]'', the Professor Oak's Lecture segments include the New Pokédex numbers of {{p|Slowpoke}}, {{p|Starmie}}, and {{p|Marowak}} (80, 168, and 204, respectively), which are referred to as "Pokémon GS Numbers".

==In merchandise==
[[File:New Numbers sticker sheet.png|thumb|150px|right|American Greetings stickers (including {{p|Stantler}}'s Japanese name)]]
In a Pokémon sticker set by {{wp|American Greetings}}, the New Pokédex numbers are used.

==Trivia==
* The New Pokédex and [[List of Pokémon by Johto Pokédex number|its expanded form]] are the only regional Pokédexes to include all the Pokémon from multiple [[generation]]s, specifically all [[Generation I]] and {{gen|II}} Pokémon.
* The New Pokédex was the last regional Pokédex to include all Pokémon that existed at the time.
* {{p|Celebi}} is the only Pokémon to have the same number (#251) in both the New Pokédex and the [[National Pokédex]].
